{"abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system based on just intonation, using exact integer frequency ratios.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"JustIntonation","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning14JustIntonationV","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"JustIntonation","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"JustIntonation","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"JustIntonation","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/UsingIvorTuning"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A just intonation system is defined by a set of frequency ratios relative to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tonic, each derived from small-integer harmonics. Any number of tones per interval of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equivalence is supported — from a simple pentatonic to Harry Partch’s 43-tone 11-limit scale.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On initialization, ratios outside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[1, equivalenceRatio)"},{"text":" are reduced by dividing by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalenceRatio"},{"text":" until they fall in range; exact multiples of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalenceRatio"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(including 1:1) are silently discarded. The remaining ratios are deduplicated and sorted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios"},{"text":" property prepends the tonic (1:1) and appends the interval of equivalence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so it always spans one complete interval of equivalence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does not support standard pitch notation. Just intonation systems are too variable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to map reliably to the 35 pitch classes of standard notation: even 5-limit scales","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contain enharmonic pairs that are distinct in just intonation but share a single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spelling, and higher-limit systems diverge further or exceed the 35-pitch-class maximum.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/init(ratios:equivalenceRatio:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/equivalenceRatio","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/TuningSystem-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/